yMORE HISTORY             (PAGE 2)

g   NOW ADVENTURERS EXPEDITION INTO
THE DUNGEONS IN SEARCH OF OLD
MAGICAL TREASURES, AND MONEY. THEY
FIND NO ALLIES, AND FIND THEY MUST
BATTLE EVERYTHING THEY MEET.

r   THE MOST DESIREABLE TARGETS OF
THESE ADVENTURERS ARE THE SHADOW
MONSTERS WHO ARE THE LEADERS OF EACH
SECTION. EACH SHADOW MONSTER HAS A
SPECIAL POWERFUL ONE-OF-A-KIND ITEM
WHICH IS OF GREAT USE.

b   IT IS ALSO SAID, THAT AT SOME
POINT IN THE PAST THERE WAS NO
MAGIC. FEW BELIEVE THIS MYTH, BUT
THOSE WHO DO, BELIEVE THAT ANCIENT
PEOPLE HAD A THING CALLED 'SIENSE'
THAT WAS SORT OF LIKE MAGIC.

o   BACK IN THE 'SIENSE' DAYS, THERE
WERE GREAT UNDERGROUND CITIES WITH
HUGE MECHANICAL STRUCTURES MOVING
THROUGH GIANT STREETS, BETWEEN HUGE
HOUSES THAT WERE MANY STORIES HIGH.

yHIT ANY KEY...
eX
g   THESE GREAT MOVING STRUCTURES
WERE USUALLY OWNED BY MERCHANTS WHO
TRAVELLED THE UNDERWORLD, BUYING
FROM HUGE FACTORIES, AND SELLING TO
HUGE MARKETPLACES THAT WERE CALLED
SUPER-STORES, AND WERE RUN BY
'EMBAS'. THERE WERE ALSO 'LAWERS',
BUT NO ONE KNOWS WHAT THEY WERE FOR.

r   THE ANCIENT MANUSCRIPT THAT
CONTAINS THIS KNOWLEDGE IS CALLED
'MERCHANTS OF THE UNDERWORLD.' WHOLE
RELIGIONS HAVE DEVELOPED AROUND IT.

b   A COMPETING MANUSCRIPT PREDICTS
THAT IN THE FUTURE, THE CREATURES
THAT INHABIT THE DUNGEONS WILL FIND
A HUGE OPEN WORLD, IN WHICH A SUN
SHINES BRIGHTLY IN THE SKY, AND
THERE ARE MOUNTAINS, FORESTS,
STREAMS, AND OCEANS TO EXPLORE AND
ENJOY. SOME BELIEVE THAT THEY WILL
BE ABLE TO LEAVE THE DARKNESS OF
THE DUNGEONS OF THE NEW WORLD, BUT
SOME BELIEVE THAT MOST WILL STILL
SPEND ALL THEIR TIME IN DARK, DANK
DUNGEONS. THE WORLD IS CALLED
MORAFF'S WORLD.

